From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 07:55:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/39] Built-in browser: no files, no pages on this machine or
 its network

The web and media floaters, prim and parcel media and parcel music all
load through CEF. A program driving the viewer can type into an open
browser window, so a check where LEAP calls arrive isn't enough: the
viewer itself now refuses file: URLs (also behind view-source:) and
pages on this machine or its network: loopback, private, link-local and
shared (100.64/10) IPv4 addresses in any of the forms a browser reads
(127.1, 2130706433, 0x7f.0.0.1, percent-encoded), localhost names, and
any IPv6 literal. The grid's own login page and login service are
allowed, wherever the grid runs.

Checked in LLViewerMediaImpl::navigateInternal before the MIME type
probe requests anything, in LLPluginClassMedia::loadURI before any
plugin gets a URL, and when a page's address changes (a link, form or
redirect inside it got there; that request has gone out by then): the
page is replaced with about:blank. A refusal shows a notice and posts
IbashoEvents {event: "refused", what: "browser"}, at most once a minute
for the same reason.

Not covered: host names that resolve to local addresses, and requests a
page makes for its parts (images, scripts, frames).
